#* {{zh-q|答問 如 響，應聲 而 出，於是 ^溫 大 敬服。|{{w|Qin Mi}}'s answered every question as quickly as an '''echo''' follows a sound. Upon hearing his answers, {{w|Zhang Wen (Eastern Wu)|Zhang Wen}} came to admire and esteem him greatly.|ref=Sanguozhi}}
#* {{zh-q|每 至 晴 初 霜 旦，林 寒 澗 肅，常 有 高 猿 長 嘯，屬{zhǔ} 引 淒 異，空 谷 傳 響，哀 轉 久 絕。|On frosty mornings, the sky clear at dawn, the woods and mountain brooks are shrouded in a desolate chill and stillness. High above, apes and monkeys oft let out prolonged cries, '''echoing''' one after another, piercingly sorrowful. The empty valleys reverberate with their mournful wails, lingering in the air for a long time before fading away.|ref=Shuijingzhu}}
#* {{zh-q|得意 高歌，<br>夜 靜 聲 偏 朗。<br>無人 賞，<br>自家 拍掌，<br>唱 徹 千 山 響。|In high spirits, loudly I sing,<br>Swelling the tranquil night with full-bodied sound.<br>No one praises me;<br>I clap my hands alone,<br>And a thousand mountains '''echo''' my song and applause.|CI|ref={{circa2|18<sup>th</sup> century|short=y}}, 釋正喦,{{lw|zh|s:銅鼓書堂詞話|點絳脣|pref=《|suf=》}}<br>Tr. {{w|zh:初大告|Chu Dagao}}}}
